      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Clusters 1–3 were obtained by reaction of Ln(acac)3·2H2O (0.03 mmol; Ln = Tb for 1) and HL (0.03 mmol) in a mixed solvent of 25 mL acetonitrile and 6 mL CH2Cl2. The ensuing yellow solution was stirred at 70 °C and then cooled to room temperature. After filtration, the solution was left unperturbed to evaporate slowly, giving yellow block crystals suitable for single-crystal X-ray diffraction after about 5 days.",
